-- title:
--   Orbit centre generates (σ₁varpiₜ,X₀,X₁) in the Drinfeld chart
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\ne q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise images (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)) of the function field of $X_H$ over $\mathbb Q$ at level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   **The base ring and the chart.** Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring, a domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and with $\xi$ in the image of $A\to L$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function transported to $L$. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=qu$ for some unit $u$ (hypothesis `hϖt`). Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the finite chart, the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlg A ↥K {j}` of $K$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A ↥K j` given by $j$, and let $X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of the two charts, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$ (hypotheses `hy`, `hϖy`). The hypothesis `hss` asserts that $y$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Let $z$ be a point of $X$, let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` (hypothesis `hϖz`), and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ (hypothesis `hz`). Let $y'$ be a point of `XFin A ↥K j` $=\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` $(y')=z$ (hypothesis `hy'`), subject to the same supersingularity condition `hss'` for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and assume `hy'y` : $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld local chart.** Let $W_1$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal) and $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$. Let $f_1,u_1,v_1\in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1\equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W₁`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and let
--   $$e_1:\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\big/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\big)$$
--   be a ring isomorphism of the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk with this quotient. Throughout, `toC` is the canonical map $\mathcal O_{X,z}\to\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$, `mkS` the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` the ring homomorphism $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ given by the germ at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin`; write $\Psi:=e_1\circ\mathtt{toC}\circ\mathtt{germY}:C\to S$, and set
--   $$\mathfrak M:=\big(\mathtt{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi),\ \mathtt{mkS}\,X_0,\ \mathtt{mkS}\,X_1\big),\qquad \mathfrak N:=\big(\mathtt{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\ \mathtt{mkS}\,X_0,\ \mathtt{mkS}\,X_1\big).$$
--   For $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ and $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$, the predicate [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) says that $\tau$ realises the action of $\gamma^{-1}$ on the modular function field: for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\ne0$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi)=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the Laurent expansion of $\tau x$ pushed to $\mathbb C$ by $\iota$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\gamma^{-1}$ conjugated by the scaling matrix of level $q\ell$, equals the corresponding expansion for $f$.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hW₁`** is a conjunction of seven clauses about these data. (i) For every $a\in A$, $e_1$ carries the image of $a$ in the completed stalk to $\mathtt{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1 a)$. (ii) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$. (iii) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ and every such $\tau$ preserving $C$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. (iv) For every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W_1$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W_1)$ such that $\theta\circ\Psi=\Psi\circ\tau$ on $C$; $\theta$ fixes all constants $\mathtt{mkS}\,C(w)$; $\theta(\mathtt{mkS}\,X_j)\equiv\sum_i \mathtt{mkS}(C(M_{ij})X_i)$ modulo $(\mathtt{mkS}\,X_0,\mathtt{mkS}\,X_1)^2$; $c^{q+1}\equiv1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$; $c\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$; and $c-1\notin\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$. (v) For all integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and all primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting at least one of $\mathtt{mkS}\,X_0,\mathtt{mkS}\,X_1$, each containing $\mathtt{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi)$, and each containing an element $a_kX_0+b_kX_1+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ along $e_1\circ\mathtt{toC}$ are distinct. (vi) For every prime $P$ of $S$ omitting one of $\mathtt{mkS}\,X_0,\mathtt{mkS}\,X_1$, containing $\mathtt{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi)$ and containing an element $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, and every $a\in C$: $\Psi(a)\in P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$ in $L$. (vii) There exist a proof that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, an element $a_0\in A$ with the difference of that element of $C$ and the image of $a_0$ lying in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b\in W_1$ with at least one of $a,b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0}\mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and such that $\Psi$ of that difference equals $\mathtt{mkS}\,h$.
--
--   **The orbit centre and the remaining hypotheses.** Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ which, by `hJ`, is the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $(\tau|_C)^{-1}\big(\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak N)\big)$, taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. Assume further: `hcstab`, that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y$, and every $a\in C$, one has $\Psi(a)\in\mathfrak N$ if and only if $\Psi(\tau a)\in\mathfrak N$; `hcen`, that $\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak M)=y$; `hdense`, that for every $n\in\mathbb N$ and every $s\in S$ there is $a\in C$ with $\Psi(a)-s\in\mathfrak M^n$; `hres`, that every element of $C$ is congruent modulo $y$ to the image of an element of $A$; and `hSmax`, that $\mathfrak M$ is maximal and is the only maximal ideal of $S$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the following four assertions hold:
--
--   1. $\Psi(J)$ generates $\mathfrak N$, that is, `Ideal.map` $\Psi\,J=\big(\mathtt{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t),\mathtt{mkS}\,X_0,\mathtt{mkS}\,X_1\big)$;
--
--   2. there is an ideal $I$ of $C$ with $J=\Psi^{-1}(\mathfrak N)\cap I$ and $I+y=C$;
--
--   3. $J\le y$;
--
--   4. the image of $\varpi_t$ under $A\to C$ lies in $J$.
--
--   This is the step which identifies the centre of the blow-up used to construct the auxiliary level structure at a supersingular point of the integral model: the globally defined ideal $J$, obtained by intersecting the pullbacks of the Drinfeld-chart ideal $(\sigma_1\varpi_t,X_0,X_1)$ over the finite family of level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, is shown to generate that ideal after completion, to agree with it locally at $y$ up to a factor comaximal with $y$, to be contained in $y$, and to contain $\varpi_t$. It is used by the subsequent statements on the blow-up chart, its Drinfeld fibre, the action of level automorphisms on it, and the primes lying over supersingular points.
